The WCD calculation is based on the Network Calculus method, using the following equation:

WCD = (frame_size + overhead) / bandwidth + propagation_delay + switching_delay + time_synchronization_error

where:

* frame_size is the size of the frame in bytes
* overhead is the overhead of the frame in bytes (e.g. headers, trailers)
* bandwidth is the bandwidth of the link in bits per second
* propagation_delay is the propagation delay of the link in seconds
* switching_delay is the switching delay of the switch in seconds
* time_synchronization_error is the time synchronization error in seconds

The CBS parameters used are:

* bandwidth: 100 Mbps
* periodicity: varies per flow (in microseconds)
* deadline: varies per flow (in microseconds)
* payload: varies per flow (in bytes)

The IdleSlope and SendSlope are calculated based on the given IdleSlope value of 75%.

